<given-names>RW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Defining and detecting malaria epidemics in the highlands of western Kenya</article-title><source>Emerg Infect Dis</source><year>2002</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>555</fpage><lpage>562</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12023909</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Najera</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Prevention and control of malaria epidemics</article-title><source>Parassitologia</source><year>1999</year><volume>41</volume><fpage>339</fpage><lpage>347</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10697881</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pavlin</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Investigation of disease outbreaks detected by "syndromic" surveillance systems</article-title><source>J Urban Health</source><year>2003</year><volume>80</volume><fpage>i107</fpage><lpage>i114</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12791785</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>le Sueur</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Sharp</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Appleton</surname><given-names>CC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A historical perspective of the malaria problem in Natal with emphasis on the period 1928 - 1932</article-title><source>S Afr J Sci</source><year>1993</year><volume>89</volume><fpage>232</fpage><lpage>239</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sharp</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>le Sueur</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Malaria in South Afri